 1681: Across the five public windows selected by the minority-positive prevalence criterion, the arithmetic mean of window-level macro-F1 is 0.8949, with a range from 0.8536 to 0.9226. Pooling their confusion matrices gives 82,292 TN, 2,355 FP, 2,937 FN, and 12,416 TP over 100,000 flows. The resulting pooled macro-F1 is 0.8966, class-1 F1 is 0.8243, and FPR is 2.7821\%. This pooled macro-F1 is not identical to the mean window-level score because the former is recomputed after aggregating counts. A pooled PR-AUC or ROC-AUC is not claimed here because those ranking measures require concatenated flow-level probabilities rather than confusion-matrix counts.
